{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: RNA-only, PCA-2000, single profile, ~48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether adding image data provides any signal at all in this multimodal cellular profiling task. config_008 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, no aggregation, concat fusion) directly tests this by keeping the RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical to the baseline, while introducing the minimal set of new variables required to add an image modality (ResNet50 + simple concat). This isolates the effect of modality/fusion as much as possible without confounding with encoder choice or profile complexity. If it substantially outperforms 48.5%, we know images carry complementary signal and can then explore better encoders/fusion. If it does not, we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder improvements or multiprofile settings. Testing an image-only baseline first would be informative but delays the practically central question of whether the multimodal combination works, and testing a more complex multimodal config (e.g., multiprofile + transformer aggregation) would confound too many variables with only one reference point."
}

